course: dictionary
lesson: 9481
title: Steadily: slow, even and calm
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Steadily» tells you how something happens: slowly and evenly, without stopping or sudden changes. «The rain fell steadily all afternoon.» The rain did not pour down in a rush, and it did not stop and start. It kept going at the same gentle pace. To check, put your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: The word can also mean firmly and calmly, without shaking. «She looked at the frightened puppy steadily» means she kept her eyes on it calmly and did not flinch. The clue is the feeling in the sentence: calm, not jumpy.
explain: Look for clue words around it, such as slowly, evenly, regularly or without a break. A runner who runs steadily keeps the same pace from start to finish. A runner who sprints, then stops, then sprints again has not run steadily.
fact: Steadily means in a slow, even and regular way, without stopping or sudden changes.
fact: Steadily can also mean firmly and calmly, without shaking, as in looking at someone steadily.
fact: In maths, a number that grows steadily goes up by about the same amount each time, making a straight line on a graph.
fact: «The tortoise walked steadily on» and won the race, while the hare ran in fast bursts and stopped to nap.
fact: Stars spend most of their lives steadily turning hydrogen into helium, and seen from space, above the air, they shine steadily.
exercise: «The rain fell steadily all afternoon.» What does steadily mean here? | Backwards and upside down | In a loud, sudden burst | *In a slow, even way, without stopping or sudden changes | Very cold and icy
exercise: Ella says steadily means fast and jumpy. Is she right? | *No, it means slow and even, without sudden changes | Yes, it means loud and noisy | Yes, it means fast and jumpy | No, it means sleepy
exercise: «She looked at the frightened puppy steadily.» What does steadily suggest about her? | *She was calm and firm, and did not shake | She was rushing and frightened | She was asleep | She was loud and angry
test: «A number that grows steadily goes up by about the same amount each time.» On a graph, what shape does steady growth make? | A zigzag that jumps up and down | *A straight line | A circle | A single dot
test: «The tortoise walked steadily on and won the race.» Why did the tortoise win? | It flew over the hare | *It kept a slow, even pace without stopping | It ran in sudden bursts | It hid until the very end
exam: Which sentence uses steadily to mean firmly and calmly, without shaking? | «The wind blew wildly through the trees.» | «The bus stopped suddenly at the corner.» | *«Her hand held the camera steadily, so the photo was sharp.» | «The children ran off in all directions.»
